-- A PERFECTLY ORDINARY ERRAND
--
-- You are a real person. You have a library book that is due back. That is the whole of your
-- ambition today and it is a reasonable one.
--
-- The building disagrees with you about almost everything else.
--
-- This is a first person game with a real window: every turn the view you are standing in is
-- drawn, saved as a picture, and shown in a window that keeps up with it by itself. The walls are
-- cast a ray at a time, the things in the rooms are drawn as flat pictures turned to face you, and
-- the writing on the screen is drawn dot by dot out of PoliteLang's own letters. Nothing is
-- fetched from anywhere.
--
-- Written in PoliteLang by Creeperdiamonds Studios.


please use "parts/world.polite"
please use "parts/people.polite"


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The view
--
-- The screen is three hundred dots across and a hundred and sixty down:
--
--     0 to 9      a bar saying where you are and what you are carrying
--     10 to 111   what you can see, with the horizon at 61
--     112 down    what just happened, in words
--
-- One ray is cast for each of the three hundred columns. Rather than creep forward in tiny steps,
-- each ray jumps straight to the next line of the grid it would cross, so it takes about twenty
-- jumps to cross the whole building instead of several hundred small ones. Which line it crossed
-- last also says which face of the wall it struck, and the two faces are lit differently, which is
-- the whole reason a corner looks like a corner.
--
-- What comes back is the distance to the wall in every column, which is what tells the things in
-- the room whether they are in front of the wall or behind it.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

please define the walls seen with a rows and an ex and a why and a facing:
    remember depth is an empty list

    repeat for every column from 0 to 299:
        remember angle is facing minus 0.55 plus column times 0.003667
        remember dx is the cosine of angle
        remember dy is the sine of angle

        remember cellx is the rounded down version of ex
        remember celly is the rounded down version of why

        -- How far along the ray it costs to cross one whole square each way.
        remember stridex is the size of (1 divided by dx or 999999)
        remember stridey is the size of (1 divided by dy or 999999)

        remember stepx is 1
        remember runx is 0.0
        check if dx is under 0:
            change stepx to 0 minus 1
            change runx to (ex minus cellx) times stridex
        otherwise:
            change runx to (cellx plus 1 minus ex) times stridex
        thank you for checking

        remember stepy is 1
        remember runy is 0.0
        check if dy is under 0:
            change stepy to 0 minus 1
            change runy to (why minus celly) times stridey
        otherwise:
            change runy to (celly plus 1 minus why) times stridey
        thank you for checking

        remember flat is no
        remember stuff is "#"
        remember jumps is 0
        keep going forever:
            change jumps to jumps plus 1
            check if jumps is over 90:
                stop repeating
            thanks
            check if runx is under runy:
                change runx to runx plus stridex
                change cellx to cellx plus stepx
                change flat to no
            otherwise:
                change runy to runy plus stridey
                change celly to celly plus stepy
                change flat to yes
            thank you for checking
            change stuff to the stuff at with cellx and celly and rows
            check if stuff is not ".":
                stop repeating
            thanks
        thanks

        -- Backing off the last jump gives the distance straight ahead rather than along the ray,
        -- which is what stops the walls bulging outward at the edges of the screen.
        remember far is 0.05
        check if flat:
            change far to runy minus stridey
        otherwise:
            change far to runx minus stridex
        thank you for checking
        check if far is under 0.05:
            change far to 0.05
        thanks
        add far to depth

        remember high is the rounded version of 90 divided by far or 90
        remember half is high kept between 1 and 50
        remember paint is the paint of with stuff
        remember lit is 1.0
        check if flat:
            change lit to 0.64
        thanks
        remember shade is ((1 minus far divided by 22) kept between 0.16 and 1) times lit
        remember rr is the rounded version of (item 1 of paint or 130) times shade
        remember gg is the rounded version of (item 2 of paint or 130) times shade
        remember bb is the rounded version of (item 3 of paint or 130) times shade
        draw a line from the point column and 61 minus half to the point column and 61 plus half in the colour with red rr green gg blue bb
    thanks

    give back depth
thank you for defining


-- One thing in the room, drawn as a small picture turned to face you.
--
-- How far ahead of you it is decides how big it is drawn; how far to one side decides where
-- across. Each column of it is only drawn if it is nearer than the wall behind that column, which
-- is what lets a thing stand properly behind a corner.
please define a thing shown with a shape and a forward and a side and a depth:
    remember sx is 150 plus (side divided by forward or 0) times 244.7
    remember high is 90 divided by forward or 90
    remember picture is the shape called with shape
    remember down is the number of items in picture
    remember across is the length of (item 1 of picture or ".")
    remember cell is (high times 0.95) divided by down or 1
    check if cell is under 0.4:
        change cell to 0.4
    thanks

    remember foot is 61 plus high divided by 2
    remember left is sx minus (cell times across) divided by 2
    remember paint is the colour of a with shape
    remember shade is (1 minus forward divided by 22) kept between 0.2 and 1
    remember baser is item 1 of paint or 190
    remember baseg is item 2 of paint or 190
    remember baseb is item 3 of paint or 190

    repeat for every c from 0 to across minus 1:
        remember colx is the rounded version of left plus c times cell
        check if (colx is under 300) and not (colx is under 0):
            remember behind is item colx plus 1 of depth or 999
            check if forward is under behind:
                remember colright is the rounded version of left plus (c plus 1) times cell minus 1
                check if colright is under colx:
                    change colright to colx
                thanks
                repeat for every r from 0 to down minus 1:
                    remember line is item r plus 1 of picture or ""
                    remember mark is the letter c plus 1 of line or "."
                    check if mark is not ".":
                        remember lift is 0
                        check if mark is "o":
                            change lift to 52
                        otherwise if mark is "*":
                            change lift to 0 minus 46
                        thank you for checking
                        remember rr is the rounded version of baser times shade plus lift
                        remember gg is the rounded version of baseg times shade plus lift
                        remember bb is the rounded version of baseb times shade plus lift
                        remember boxtop is the rounded version of foot minus (down minus r) times cell
                        remember boxlow is the rounded version of foot minus (down minus r minus 1) times cell
                        fill a box from the point colx and boxtop to the point colright and boxlow in the colour with red rr green gg blue bb
                    thanks
                thanks
            thanks
        thanks
    thanks
thank you for defining


-- The building seen from above, small, in the corner. Two dots to a square.
please define the little map with a rows and an ex and a why:
    fill a box from the point 236 and 12 to the point 295 and 57 in the colour with red 12 green 14 blue 20
    repeat for every down from 0 to 20:
        repeat for every across from 0 to 27:
            remember stuff is the stuff at with across and down and rows
            remember left is 238 plus across times 2
            remember top is 14 plus down times 2
            check if stuff is ".":
                fill a box from the point left and top to the point left plus 1 and top plus 1 in the colour with red 58 green 64 blue 78
            otherwise:
                fill a box from the point left and top to the point left plus 1 and top plus 1 in the colour with red 120 green 126 blue 140
            thank you for checking
        thanks
    thanks
    remember mex is 238 plus (the whole part of ex) times 2
    remember mwhy is 14 plus (the whole part of why) times 2
    fill a box from the point mex minus 1 and mwhy minus 1 to the point mex plus 2 and mwhy plus 2 in the colour with red 240 green 196 blue 64
thank you for defining


-- Which of the sixteen ways round you are looking. Turning always lands on one of these, so a
-- direction can be named, and so that turning right four times and left four times leaves you
-- looking at exactly what you started at rather than nearly at it.
please define the way named with a way:
    remember points is an empty list
    add "east" to points
    add "east south east" to points
    add "south east" to points
    add "south south east" to points
    add "south" to points
    add "south south west" to points
    add "south west" to points
    add "west south west" to points
    add "west" to points
    add "west north west" to points
    add "north west" to points
    add "north north west" to points
    add "north" to points
    add "north north east" to points
    add "north east" to points
    add "east north east" to points
    give back item way plus 1 of points or "east"
thank you for defining


-- The same sixteen headings in their short form, for the bar along the top.
please define the way lettered with a way:
    remember points is an empty list
    add "E" to points
    add "ESE" to points
    add "SE" to points
    add "SSE" to points
    add "S" to points
    add "SSW" to points
    add "SW" to points
    add "WSW" to points
    add "W" to points
    add "WNW" to points
    add "NW" to points
    add "NNW" to points
    add "N" to points
    add "NNE" to points
    add "NE" to points
    add "ENE" to points
    give back item way plus 1 of points or "E"
thank you for defining


-- Words broken into lines that fit the panel.
please define the lines of with a saying and a room:
    remember lines is an empty list
    remember line is ""
    for every word in the words in saying:
        remember tryout is word
        check if line is not "":
            change tryout to "{line} {word}"
        thanks
        check if (the length of tryout) is over room:
            add line to lines
            change line to word
        otherwise:
            change line to tryout
        thank you for checking
    thanks
    check if line is not "":
        add line to lines
    thanks
    give back lines
thank you for defining


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Setting out
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

please remember rows is the building
please remember cast is the folk
please remember acrosses is the acrosses
please remember downs is the downs

-- The names of everything that has been picked up and is no longer standing there.
please remember gone is an empty list

please remember ex is 3.5
please remember why is 3.5
please remember way is 0
please remember bag is an empty list
please remember note is "You are late returning a library book. Your own front door is straight ahead of you. Nothing else about today is going to be as straightforward as that sentence."
please remember playing is yes
please remember won is no

please open a canvas 300 across and 160 down
please make each dot 4 across

please show ""
please show "  A PERFECTLY ORDINARY ERRAND"
please show ""
please show "  You have a library book. It is due back. That is all you want."
please show ""
please show "  w  walk forward      a  turn left       look   at what is in front of you"
please show "  s  step back         d  turn right      talk   to it"
please show "                                          take   it"
please show "                                          give   it what you are carrying"
please show "                                          bag    what you have"
please show "                                          done   give up on the errand"
please show ""

please keep going forever:
    check if not playing:
        stop repeating
    thanks

    remember facing is way times 0.3926991

    -- The ceiling darkens upward and the floor darkens downward, away from the horizon.
    repeat for every band from 0 to 50:
        remember lift is the rounded version of band times 0.5
        draw a line from the point 0 and 10 plus band to the point 299 and 10 plus band in the colour with red 16 plus lift green 19 plus lift blue 26 plus lift
        remember fall is the rounded version of (50 minus band) times 0.5
        draw a line from the point 0 and 61 plus band to the point 299 and 61 plus band in the colour with red 38 plus fall green 33 plus fall blue 27 plus fall
    thanks

    remember depth is the walls seen with rows and ex and why and facing

    -- How far away each thing is, kept once so it is not worked out again and again below.
    remember aways is an empty list
    repeat for every n from 1 to the number of items in cast:
        remember tx is (item n of acrosses or 0) plus 0.5
        remember ty is (item n of downs or 0) plus 0.5
        add ((tx minus ex) times (tx minus ex)) plus ((ty minus why) times (ty minus why)) to aways
    thanks

    -- Furthest first, so that a nearer thing paints over one behind it. Each turn round the loop
    -- takes the furthest thing that is still nearer than the one taken last time.
    remember cutoff is 999999.0
    repeat for every pass from 1 to the number of items in cast:
        remember worst is 0
        remember worstaway is 0 minus 1
        repeat for every n from 1 to the number of items in cast:
            check if not (gone contains (the part with (item n of cast or "") and 1)):
                remember away is item n of aways or 0
                check if (away is under cutoff) and (away is over worstaway):
                    change worstaway to away
                    change worst to n
                thanks
            thanks
        thanks
        check if worst is over 0:
            change cutoff to worstaway
            remember tx is (item worst of acrosses or 0) plus 0.5
            remember ty is (item worst of downs or 0) plus 0.5
            remember rx is tx minus ex
            remember ry is ty minus why
            remember forward is rx times (the cosine of facing) plus ry times (the sine of facing)
            check if forward is over 0.35:
                remember side is ry times (the cosine of facing) minus rx times (the sine of facing)
                a thing shown with (the part with (item worst of cast or "") and 2) and forward and side and depth
            thanks
        thanks
    thanks

    the little map with rows and ex and why

    -- The bar along the top, and the panel along the bottom.
    fill a box from the point 0 and 0 to the point 299 and 9 in the colour with red 18 green 20 blue 27
    make the letters 1 across
    remember carrying is "carrying nothing"
    check if (the number of items in bag) is over 0:
        change carrying to "carrying {the join of bag with ", "}"
    thanks
    remember rightside is 296 minus (the width of carrying written)

    remember here is "{the room at with (the whole part of ex) and (the whole part of why)}  {the way lettered with way}"
    remember room is the rounded down version of (rightside minus 10) divided by 6
    check if (the length of here) is over room:
        change here to the piece of here from 1 to (room kept between 1 and 90)
    thanks

    write here at the point 4 and 2 in the colour with red 226 green 208 blue 150
    write carrying at the point rightside and 2 in the colour with red 150 green 196 blue 226

    fill a box from the point 0 and 112 to the point 299 and 159 in the colour with red 18 green 20 blue 27
    draw a line from the point 0 and 112 to the point 299 and 112 in the colour with red 70 green 76 blue 92
    remember lines is the lines of with note and 49
    repeat for every n from 1 to 5:
        write item n of lines or "" at the point 5 and 108 plus n times 9 in the colour with red 214 green 216 blue 220
    thanks

    try to:
        save the canvas to "errand.png"
        put the canvas in a window
    otherwise if it does not work out:
        show "  (the window is not available here, so this is the terminal only)"
    thank you for trying

    -- Whatever you are nearest to is what the words act on.
    remember near is 0
    remember bestaway is 2.6
    repeat for every n from 1 to the number of items in cast:
        check if not (gone contains (the part with (item n of cast or "") and 1)):
            remember away is the square root of (item n of aways or 0) or 99
            check if away is under bestaway:
                change bestaway to away
                change near to n
            thanks
        thanks
    thanks

    remember entry is item near of cast or ""
    remember name is the part with entry and 1
    remember wants is the part with entry and 4
    remember gives is the part with entry and 5

    show ""
    show "  {note}"
    check if near is over 0:
        show ""
        show "  Near you: {name}"
    thanks
    show ""
    ask "  > " as said
    change said to the small letters of the trimmed version of said

    remember step is 0.42
    check if said is "w":
        remember nx is ex plus (the cosine of facing) times step
        remember ny is why plus (the sine of facing) times step
        check if not (a wall at with nx and ny and rows):
            change ex to nx
            change why to ny
            change note to "You walk on."
        otherwise:
            change note to "The wall stays where it is. You have tried this in other buildings and it has always gone this way."
        thank you for checking
    otherwise if said is "s":
        remember bx is ex minus (the cosine of facing) times step
        remember by is why minus (the sine of facing) times step
        check if not (a wall at with bx and by and rows):
            change ex to bx
            change why to by
            change note to "You step back."
        otherwise:
            change note to "There is a wall behind you as well. It is a building. This is what they do."
        thank you for checking
    otherwise if said is "a":
        change way to way minus 1
        check if way is under 0:
            change way to 15
        thanks
        change note to "You turn to your left, and are now looking {the way named with way}."
    otherwise if said is "d":
        change way to way plus 1
        check if way is over 15:
            change way to 0
        thanks
        change note to "You turn to your right, and are now looking {the way named with way}."
    otherwise if said is "look":
        check if near is over 0:
            change note to "You look at {name}."
        otherwise:
            change note to "There is nothing close enough to look at properly. Walk up to a thing and it will let you."
        thank you for checking
    otherwise if said is "talk":
        check if near is over 0:
            change note to the part with entry and 3
        otherwise:
            change note to "There is nobody close enough to talk to, which on the whole has been the shape of the day."
        thank you for checking
    otherwise if said is "take":
        check if near is under 1:
            change note to "There is nothing close enough to take."
        otherwise if gives is "":
            change note to "You cannot take {name}, and you suspect it would be worse if you could."
        otherwise if wants is not "":
            change note to "It will not simply be taken. It wants {wants} first."
        otherwise:
            add gives to bag
            add name to gone
            change note to "You take {gives}. Nobody stops you. Nobody was ever going to."
        thank you for checking
    otherwise if said is "give":
        check if near is under 1:
            change note to "There is nobody close enough to give anything to."
        otherwise if wants is "":
            change note to "{name} wants nothing from you. You are, in fairness, holding very little."
        otherwise if not (bag contains wants):
            change note to "It wants {wants}. You do not have {wants}."
        otherwise:
            -- Hand it over: keep everything in the bag except the one thing asked for.
            remember kept is an empty list
            for every held in bag:
                check if held is not wants:
                    add held to kept
                thanks
            thanks
            change bag to kept
            check if gives is "":
                change won to yes
                change playing to no
            otherwise:
                add gives to bag
                add name to gone
                change note to "You hand over {wants}. You are given {gives}. Neither of you remarks on it."
            thank you for checking
        thank you for checking
    otherwise if said is "bag":
        check if (the number of items in bag) is over 0:
            change note to "You are carrying: {the join of bag with ", "}. And the book, which you are always carrying."
        otherwise:
            change note to "You are carrying the library book and nothing else."
        thank you for checking
    otherwise if said is "done":
        change playing to no
    otherwise:
        change note to "The words are w, s, a, d, look, talk, take, give, bag and done."
    thank you for checking
thank you for repeating


